# Kingpin Community License v0.1

**1. Parties and coverage.** “Licensor” means Stephen A. Putman, acting personally. “Software” means the protectable material identified in the release schedule below for which Licensor expressly offers this license. “You” means the person or organization exercising the granted rights. A modification includes an adaptation that incorporates protected expression from the Software. Independent works, ideas, interfaces as such, and uses permitted by law, including fair use or fair dealing, are outside this grant wherever permission is unnecessary.

**2. Community purposes.** Personal learning, ordinary coursework (including graded assignments), independent experimentation and genuine noncommercial research, development and sharing qualify under §3, subject to §4. Individuals may collaborate, use shared facilities and publish findings. Academic supervision, grading, an unrestricted grant, a stipend, acknowledgement of support, or ordinary reports accounting for grant funds do not alone make a project directed research. An employee may experiment personally, including in their professional field, independently of assigned duties and without undertaking the work for the employer.

Voluntary donations and sponsorship that buy no access, commissioned deliverable, preferential rights or business service are compatible with a community purpose. A distributor may recover reasonable direct costs actually incurred in reproducing and delivering copies, without markup. This allowance covers such items as media and postage. It does not cover development fees, ongoing hosted access, or compensation for client work. Assess the commitments and intended beneficiaries when each covered act occurs. Incidental recognition and possible future applications do not alone determine purpose.

**3. Copyright grant.** For community purposes, Licensor grants you a worldwide, royalty-free, nonexclusive license for the copyright term, subject to §9, to reproduce and run copies, study, modify and create derivatives, and distribute or make available the original or modified Software in source or binary form. Redistribution is subject to §5, including when recovering costs under §2. You may rename a fork. Promotion, stars, sharing and feedback are voluntary. There is no requirement to publish private changes or provide source with binaries.

**4. Reserved purposes.** Separate written permission from the relevant rights holders is required to exercise licensed rights primarily for commercial advantage or compensation, including sale, commercial licensing or redistribution, incorporation in a commercial product, paid hosting or APIs, business infrastructure, procurement evaluation, commissioned development for commercial clients, and commercial white-label or OEM supply. Free access or an intermediary does not change a commercial beneficiary's purpose. Work undertaken for a client, employer or affiliate is assessed by its commissioned objective and beneficiary.

Separate written permission is also required for copies used in an organization's operations, including delivery of a live service or performance of an actual administrative, public, research-support or defense function. Independently studying a system in a sandbox can qualify under §2. Using it to administer the lab's infrastructure is operational.

Directed research requires permission when a commissioning organization controls the substantive work for its own program or is entitled to a specified research product, implementation or evaluation for its use. A paid client report qualifies even if the researcher may publish it later. Ordinary educational assessment and financial stewardship described in §2 are insufficient by themselves. Apply these rules to the work undertaken for the actual beneficiary, regardless of affiliation, funding source or institutional status. Separate written evaluation permission may be free and covers only the agreed trial. Commercial production and commercial white-label or OEM distribution require separate agreements expressly covering those rights. These boundaries apply only where licensed rights are required.

**5. Redistribution conditions.** With each distributed copy or substantial covered portion, provide this license, supplied copyright and attribution notices, and any supplied third-party notices applicable to the material distributed. Include a reasonably accessible record identifying altered files or components and summarizing changes. Credit the upstream work and identify your additions separately. A repository root, package documentation directory, or accompanying offline-readable binary licenses file suffices when it reaches the recipient. Each recipient receives a direct offer from Licensor on these terms for the covered portions. Preserve that offer and do not purport to sublicense those rights or impose inconsistent downstream terms on them.

**6. Ownership and contributions.** Each rights holder retains its rights. You may license your original additions separately if recipients can identify them and exercise their rights in the underlying Software. Distribution of a mixed work requires sufficient rights in all portions. Submission of a patch does not by itself assign copyright or authorize commercial relicensing. Integration into an owner's commercial edition requires a sufficient grant from each applicable rights holder. An upstream contribution agreement may supply that authority without transferring title. Independent forks need no upstream contribution agreement to exercise this license.

**7. Names and patents.** Accurate descriptive attribution is permitted. No trademark license or endorsement is implied. Do not represent that Licensor sponsors a fork absent permission. No express patent license is granted.

**8. Prior and third-party grants.** This license applies only to the §1 schedule. Existing grants continue on their own terms, including CC BY-NC 4.0 for kingpin-runtime@0.1.0-rc.4. No KCL condition attaches to rights exercised solely under those grants. Other dependencies retain their own terms.

**9. Breach and cure.** Rights under this grant terminate upon breach of its conditions. Stop exercising them until reinstated. On a first breach, rights reinstate automatically upon full cure within 30 calendar days after you discover that breach (the day after discovery is day one), including correcting notices and supplying corrections to affected recipients where reasonably practicable. Otherwise reinstatement requires written permission. Reinstatement does not waive claims for earlier acts. Prior compliant recipients keep their direct grants. Ownership, disclaimers and accrued claims survive termination.

**10. Warranties and liability.** To the extent permitted by applicable law, the Software is supplied as is, without express or implied warranties, including merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose and noninfringement. To that extent Licensor and contributors disclaim liability for direct, indirect, incidental, special and consequential loss arising from the Software or this license, under any theory of liability. Mandatory protections and liability that cannot lawfully be excluded remain effective.

**11. Interpretation.** Applicable law and forum are determined by ordinary legal rules. Separate commercial agreements may specify their own law and forum. If a provision is unenforceable, sever it to the extent necessary and preserve the remainder where legally possible. Only a rights holder or its authorized representative may grant separate permissions within its authority.

**Release schedule — kingpin-governed-mcp 0.1.0 developer preview.** Coverage extends only to material for which Stephen A. Putman controls the applicable rights in server.mjs, host.mjs, enforce.mjs, profiles.mjs, read-fixture.mjs, demo.mjs, acceptance.test.mjs, mcp.test.mjs and the original documentation in README.md and NOTICE.md. Preserve the original Kingpin integration credit to Stephen A. Putman. The schedule excludes independently licensed packages, the underlying runtime, external contributions outside the licensor’s control and material outside copyright protection. No rights under any preexisting grant are reduced.
